data dispatch_event_pipe_seam_note: String = "tmux pipe-pane is the one foreign-executor seam in attempt capture: upstream requires a shell-command payload. TmuxPipeCommand bounds that residue. The earlier session-environment design was rejected by live execution because pipe processes did not inherit tmux set-environment values and created no file. Staging order is state directory -> idle exact-shell pane -> default-shell -> remain-on-exit -> quoted pipe -> typed provider respawn, so the first provider byte and a fast nonzero exit are both observable. The payload itself is no longer constructed here: gunbc.dispatch_pipe_pane_emit builds it as a bash AST and renders it through the signed serializer (review 44063), which is why this module now imports a command rather than joining one."

